            {
               "text": "### The Origin of the Universe\n\nThe image in this section shows how scientists describe the history of the universe. It follows the **Lambda-CDM model**, the model used by most scientists today (<htcite0>).\n\n#### Our first explanations\n\nPeople have been trying to explain the origin of the universe for thousands of years.\n\nLong before telescopes existed, many cultures told stories about how the sky and the Earth were created. Most of these stories put people at the center — that is, they were **anthropocentric** (<htcite1>):\n- Around <htdate0>, the Babylonians described how human beings were created in the **Epic of Atrahasis**. They also told of a great flood sent as a punishment, from which Atrahasis survived, together with his wife and the animals he took with him (<htcite2>; <htcite3>; <htcite4>; <htcite5>).\n- The **Popol Vuh** was written in Mesoamerica (*Abya Yala*) between <htdate1> and <htdate2> (<htcite6>). Yet murals in El Mirador and Izapa, dated to about <htdate3>, show that the beliefs told in the Popol Vuh already existed in the region long before the book was written (<htcite7>).\n\nHumanity created other epic stories too — some of them influenced by these two (<htcite8>; <htcite9>) — but in this Atlas we will focus on these two.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a1a7c478-9061-4160-ba43-301c081733e9",
                     "text": "©ESA – C. Carreau",
