            {
               "text": "#### What do we really know?\n\nOur knowledge of the universe is quite new. Most big discoveries happened in the 20th century (<htcite0>), according to the Gregorian calendar.\n\nTwo discoveries especially helped us understand how the planet we live on was formed:\n- Edwin Hubble discovered that the universe is expanding (<htcite1>);\n- Scientists discovered the Cosmic Microwave Background — the oldest information about the universe we have ever measured (<htcite2>).\n\nYou can see both discoveries in the image above. The next texts of this *Atlas* section will explain them in detail.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "2544abb0-dc03-4654-81df-298f74faa908",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Texts with Sciences (Part I)",
